{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Perils (2nd)","html":"<article id='an4.120'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Aṅguttara Nikāya 4.120 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Numbered Discourses 4.120 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>12. Kesivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>12. With Kesi </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dutiyabhayasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Perils (2nd) </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Cattārimāni, bhikkhave, bhayāni. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, there are these four perils. </span>\n<span class='root'>Katamāni cattāri? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What four? </span>\n<span class='root'>Aggibhayaṁ, udakabhayaṁ, rājabhayaṁ, corabhayaṁ—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The perils of fire, water, kings, and bandits. </span>\n<span class='root'>Imāni kho, bhikkhave, cattāri bhayānī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>These are the four perils.” </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Kesivaggo dutiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kesi javo patodo ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nāgo ṭhānena pañcamaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Appamādo ca ārakkho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṁvejanīyañca dve bhayāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
